# Aston Martin DB5 fixed-head coupe, 1963-1965.
#
# The DB5, the DB4's Touring Superleggera body with the 4-litre engine, on sale
# from 1963 to 1965. The fixed-head coupe is modelled, not the convertible.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB5 (cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.570 x 1.680 x 1.340 m, wheelbase 2.489 m. Length, width and
# wheelbase are from the English Wikipedia DB5 article as recorded in the pack.
# **The 1.340 m height is provisional and unverified**: the commonly quoted
# figure appears in the pack but the Wikipedia infobox does not give it, so it
# is recorded here as a modelling figure only. The hull measures 4.570 m on the
# 2.489 m wheelbase (54.5 per cent) and 1.680 m wide.
#
# Shape reference: three photographs of the 1963 RM Sotheby's car. The side view
# is about 20-25 degrees forward of perpendicular with a foreshortened nose, so
# it was used qualitatively and the wheel centres fixed by the published
# wheelbase; the front three-quarter gave the grille, the covered headlamps
# under clear fairings and the bonnet scoop; the rear three-quarter gave the
# recessed plate and the **three vertically stacked round lamps per corner**,
# which are what the photograph shows and what is modelled (my brief's "wide,
# shallow tail lamps" was wrong for this car).
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found (grade d); cars of this era
# were finished to order, so the objects carry plain names: Silver Birch,
# British Racing Green, black and red. Weights silver 3, green 3, black 2,
# red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase. Chrome and the wire
# wheels keep their own materials.
#
# Speed 233 km/h, the car's quoted maximum and one of the highest of its day.
# Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60: a fast, low GT with a firm ride.
# Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1963 intro, retires staggered 1978-1981 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db5.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db5.dae (73 objects). References:
# citycars/references/aston-db5/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is squarer, the wheel openings more angular and
# the rear window less rounded than the photographed car. The glazing stands
# about 14.5-14.9 mm clear of its supporting surfaces. At 128 px the long
# bonnet, the wide grille, the covered headlamps and the fastback tail read as
# a DB5.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDB5(SilverBirch)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1963
intro_month=1
retire_year=1981
retire_month=6
speed=233
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=60
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=420

